Channel Loader composition and direct-v4 follow-up (2026-09-09)

Scope: repair and verify the real headless Loader channel fixtures after the expanded channel snapshot sweep exposed composition and protocol-version drift. This record covers channel composition and keyless replay behavior; it does not claim full browser, multi-host, coverage, real-model, or release closure.

Changes:

1. Custom-topology channel fixtures disable the default `team-delegation` Consumer when `team-run` is intentionally disabled; this prevents a provider-waiting entry from blocking Loader startup.
2. The channel-open-failure fixture registers the direct v4 adapter used by the current `TeamRun` topology and derives its orphan WAL expectation from the invitation count.
3. The direct-v4 fixture admits all endpoints before dispatch, then asserts that context delivery receipts the connected endpoint without waking its model.

